# ===========================================================================
#  .gitignore
#
#  The rule of thumb here: commit anything a human wrote or that describes how
#  the rig behaves; ignore anything a RUN produced. Test artifacts are large,
#  binary and specific to one moment in front of one console - they belong in
#  the run folder, not in history.
# ===========================================================================

# --- secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
# .env.example IS committed (it documents the variables); real keys never are.
*.env
.env
TEMP.env
!.env.example

# --- run artifacts ---------------------------------------------------------
# Every agentic run writes frames, logs and reports here. Screenshots of the
# Xbox dashboard are ~2MB each and a single run produces a dozen - committing
# them would bloat the repo permanently for evidence that is only meaningful
# alongside the run that produced it.
Xbox-Agentic-Testing/artifacts/
Xbox-Agentic-Testing/**/checkpoints.sqlite

# Scratch output from ad-hoc runs (redirected console output, etc.)
_live.txt
_lastrun.txt

# --- captured frames -------------------------------------------------------
# Screenshots are ignored everywhere EXCEPT docs/, where a handful are
# deliberately committed as reference images for the written guides.
*.png
!docs/**/*.png

Xbox-Automation-Python/capture/_probe_frames/
Xbox-Automation-Python/capture/_warmup_first_good.png

# --- temporary / experimental ----------------------------------------------
TEMP_*
TEMP_agent_run/

# NOTE on the underscore-prefixed scripts in Xbox-Agentic-Testing/ - they ARE
# committed on purpose. `_smoke_test.py`, `_test_fixes.py`, `_diagnose_capture.py`,
# `_check_ocr.py`, `_inspect_run.py` and `_verify_report.py` are diagnostic
# tools, not scratch files. The underscore only keeps them visually separate
# from the framework itself.

# --- python ----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- editors / OS ----------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# --- model caches ----------------------------------------------------------
# PaddleOCR downloads ~200MB of models on first use.
.paddleocr/
paddleocr_models/
.env